.nh
.TH "PB-AUTH-LOGIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-auth-login - Add this computer to your account, or sign in again, through browser approval


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb auth login [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add this computer to your account, or sign in again, through browser approval

.PP
Print an approval link and open it when a browser is available. Sign in through WorkOS on this or another device, choose the workspace and explicitly approve; a computer that is not on your account yet is added to that workspace. No local callback listener or copied token is needed. Interrupted attempts resume securely; the existing account remains active until replacement succeeds.

.PP
Sign-in credentials are stored in the selected local profile for its configured Paperboat server. Account commands use that profile; a missing or rejected session must be repaired with pb auth login before protected resources can be used.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--change-account\fP[=false]
	sign in with another account after browser approval

.PP
\fB--fresh\fP[=false]
	remove this computer's setup and machine record, then add it again

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for login

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print approval and sign-in states as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-browser\fP[=false]
	print the approval link without opening a browser

.PP
\fB--reauth\fP[=false]
	authenticate the current account again


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-auth(1)\fP
